{"availability":"available","full":"tusharbeckham/solar-forecast","name":"solar-forecast","description":"Most solar forecasters throw raw ML at the weather. This one doesn't - a clear-sky physics model + plane-of-array transposition set the baseline, and ML learns only the residual. Beats clear-sky and persistence (0.85 / 0.69 skill) on real data. Python, scikit-learn, live Streamlit demo.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-08T10:50:33Z","updated":"2026-07-09T20:54:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://solar-forecast.streamlit.app/","topics":["data-science","energy-forecasting","machine-learning","physics-informed-machine-learning","pvlib","python","renewable-energy","scientific-computing","scikit-learn","solar-energy","solar-power-forecasting","time-series-forecasting"],"demo":"https://solar-forecast.streamlit.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:32:43.190Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:32:43.190Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:32:43.190Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:44:45.800Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T07:32:43.190Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Physics-informed machine learning for solar PV output forecasting — a physical clear-sky model sets the baseline, and machine learning learns only the weather-driven correction.","I built this to forecast solar PV output from weather — and to learn physics-informed ML hands-on. Rather than making a model learn everything from scratch, I give it a physical clear-sky baseline (what a panel should produce on a cloudless day) and let ML learn only the residual — the part clouds and temperature change. Final forecast = clearsky + residual(features), clipped >= 0.","Pure ML has to relearn physics it could simply be told. By encoding the sun's geometry and clear-sky irradiance directly, the model only learns the weather-driven deviation — which is more data-efficient, more interpretable, and degrades gracefully to the physical baseline when the model is unsure. This is also the natural on-ramp to a Physics-Informed Neural Network (see the roadmap)."],"features":["Physics + ML hybrid — a self-contained clear-sky irradiance model and plane-of-array (POA) transposition, corrected by a gradient-boosting residual model.","Beats standard baselines on real data — 0.85 skill vs the clear-sky prior and 0.69 vs a persistence baseline on a full year of hourly data.","Honest evaluation — leakage-free, forward-chaining backtest (train only on the past, test on the future).","Reproducible — one CLI (fetch / train / evaluate / plot / predict), a live, location-aware dashboard (demo), and a 20-test suite."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tusharbeckham/solar-forecast/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"746cbf4937bf30106bfcbc4e7457f8dc07e5fdae9610353bf2c149f2cec202f9","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:45.964Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:45.964Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Physics-informed machine learning for solar PV output forecasting — a physical clear-sky model sets the baseline, and machine learning learns only the weather-driven correction.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tusharbeckham/solar-forecast/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"746cbf4937bf30106bfcbc4e7457f8dc07e5fdae9610353bf2c149f2cec202f9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tusharbeckham/solar-forecast/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:45.965Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-09T20:54:05Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tusharbeckham/solar-forecast/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:45.965Z","hash":"746cbf4937bf30106bfcbc4e7457f8dc07e5fdae9610353bf2c149f2cec202f9","originalBytes":7038,"storedBytes":7038,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["clear-sky","model","docs","residual","forecast","physics","solar-